# LF everywhere, for the same reason `backend/.gitattributes` says it — and for
# one more that is specific to this deployable.
#
# `src/lib/api/generated/` is a BYTE-FOR-BYTE COPY of `backend/src/shared/`, and
# `contracts-drift.test.ts` proves it by re-running the generator with
# `--check`. The backend forces LF; without this file, Git checks the frontend
# copies out with CRLF on Windows and the comparison fails on line endings
# alone — every generated file "stale", nothing actually drifted, on a developer
# machine only. CI never saw it because a Linux checkout gives both sides LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
